---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | devsyllabus"
  description="devsyllabus privacy policy: what we collect (very little), analytics and cookies, and your choices."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />

  <div class="doc">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-09-04</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    devsyllabus is a read-only study site. Reading pages requires no
    account and collects no personal data. We do not ask for names,
    emails, or payment details except when you write to us directly, in
    which case we keep your message only to respond to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like nearly every website, our hosting provider records standard
    request logs (IP address, requested URL, timestamp, user agent) for
    security and operational purposes. These logs are retained for a
    limited period and are not used to build profiles of visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself sets no tracking cookies. Site search runs entirely
    in your browser, so search terms are not sent to or stored by us. If
    we add privacy-respecting, aggregate analytics in the future, this
    page and the <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a> will be
    updated first.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Pages link to external sources such as RFCs and documentation sites.
    Those sites have their own privacy practices, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Since we collect essentially no personal data, there is little to
    request, but if you have questions or want a message you sent us
    deleted, write to
    <a href="mailto:hello@devsyllabus.com">hello@devsyllabus.com</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    See also the <a href="/terms-of-use/">terms of use</a>,
    <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>, and
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
